{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854920-how-does-umbra-combat-works","id":854920,"title":"How does umbra combat works","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-29T01:16:42-07:00","id":854920,"title":"How does umbra combat works","content":"I'm reading the 20th rulebook and when I get to the Banes named Ooralath it says they can create a more efficient combat form in the umbra.<br /> <br /> And the stats the book provided are:<br /> Natural form:<br /> Rage 5<br /> Gnosis 3<br /> WP 7<br /> <br /> &quot;More efficient&quot; form:<br /> Strength 4<br /> Dexterity 3<br /> Stamina 3<br /> Brawl 4<br /> Dodge 2 (yes Dodge. Didn't it stop to exist!!!)<br /> <br /> Why is this &quot;more efficient&quot; form??<br /> Attack same number of dice (7)<br /> Damage one fewer die (strength 4 vs rage 5)<br /> Dodge two fewer dice.<br /> Stamina two fewer dice (stamina 3 vs rage 5)<br /> <br /> Am I understanding wrong how combat with spirits work??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11010,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","user":"erSito","date":". 03-29-2016, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T01:24:48-07:00","id":854924,"title":"","content":"It's more efficient because it's in the umbra, a.K.a it's home turf. Sorta like how a crocodile is more deadly in the water then on land.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T03:20:27-07:00","id":854964,"title":"","content":"Reading the description might help...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *Embody: This is almost identical to the Materialize<br /> Charm, save that the spirit does not build a physical body;<br /> instead, the spirit may take on a \u201cmore suitable\u201d combat<br /> form in the Umbra by spending Essence to build a body,<br /> just as if it were creating a physical form </div> </div> </div>Essentially the stats they have listed are intentionaly like that - it is not a normal spirit and does not use spirit combat stats. It comes with an always on Armor charm for bonus 4 dice of soak, which you didn't account for. It also ALWAYS has the physical form, which means that it doesn't have to spend essence to materialize (it just needs to cross over). What Embody does is that it allows you to change your shape - it means that if it faces grapple happy Garou it can grow quills. If it has to fight Garou prone to harrying it could change the quills and shoot at people... and that's just the tip oc the iceberg. It's essentially a combat adaptation charm, it's just worded a bit unclearly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T09:50:14-07:00","id":855119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854920-how-does-umbra-combat-works?p=854924#post854924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more efficient because it's in the umbra, a.K.a it's home turf. Sorta like how a crocodile is more deadly in the water then on land.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you provide some numerical/system examples? Saying a Crocodile is more deadly in the water but making it roll more dice when on the land is problem I'm pointing out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> -&gt; <br /> If it's forced into the real world it automatically takes the &quot;more suitable&quot; form. I'm OK with that.<br /> <br /> But, while in the Umbra he can choose to spend Essence (life) to take that physical form &quot;<i>the spirit may take on a \u201cmore suitable\u201d combat form</i><i> <b><u>in the Umbra</u></b> <b>by spending</b> </i><i>Essence to build a body&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It comes with an always on Armor charm for bonus 4 dice of soak </div> </div> </div>This armor is a separate power, so it works in both forms. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T13:20:04-07:00","id":855210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>erSito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854920-how-does-umbra-combat-works?p=855119#post855119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you provide some numerical/system examples? Saying a Crocodile is more deadly in the water but making it roll more dice when on the land is problem I'm pointing out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> -&gt;<br /> If it's forced into the real world it automatically takes the &quot;more suitable&quot; form. I'm OK with that.<br /> <br /> But, while in the Umbra he can choose to spend Essence (life) to take that physical form &quot;<i>the spirit may take on a \u201cmore suitable\u201d combat form</i><i> <b><u>in the Umbra</u></b> <b>by spending</b> </i><i>Essence to build a body&quot;</i><br /> <br /> This armor is a separate power, so it works in both forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have an &quot;umbral form&quot;. It has a single form that has attributes in the umbra. All that Embody does is adapt its body better to what's necessary.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T16:51:00-07:00","id":855338,"title":"","content":"I think the OP has a valid point; the math doesn't add up, and the stat block has editing artifacts in it. It's one of the weaker bits of the book. At least it stayed with WoD stats, though; one of the Fomori powers says to use Presence + Intimidate. It apparently vacationed in the Chronicles of Darkness for too long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T01:12:01-07:00","id":855563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854920-how-does-umbra-combat-works?p=855338#post855338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the OP has a valid point; the math doesn't add up, and the stat block has editing artifacts in it. It's one of the weaker bits of the book. At least it stayed with WoD stats, though; one of the Fomori powers says to use Presence + Intimidate. It apparently vacationed in the Chronicles of Darkness for too long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I agree that the author was unclear as hell, but it seems that the point for the author was that he wanted to have a spirit that had attributes and skills as a default, rather then a spirit who used normal spirit combat stats. It's one of the joys of editing in W20 :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T01:23:35-07:00","id":855572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854920-how-does-umbra-combat-works?p=855563#post855563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I agree that the author was unclear as hell, but it seems that the point for the author was that he wanted to have a spirit that had attributes and skills as a default, rather then a spirit who used normal spirit combat stats. It's one of the joys of editing in W20 :P</div> </div> </div> </div>And as the OP noted, those stats are under the bar when it comes to the spirit's base stats. Instead of being better at combat than it would be, it is worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T01:36:29-07:00","id":855576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854920-how-does-umbra-combat-works?p=855572#post855572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And as the OP noted, those stats are under the bar when it comes to the spirit's base stats. Instead of being better at combat than it would be, it is worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I saw that. But Spirits don't really get Attribute spreads. This one does. The way it's embody and burrow charms are phrased, it's actually a spirit that has a body and does not need to materialise. This is an immense boon for a spirit, as materialisation costs a stupid amount of essence, allowing these guys to have their whole essence pools, and use the Embody to just add physical traits that might work better for a certain approach.<br /> <br /> It is an obtuse way to write it, but I think it's what the author wanted to say :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T07:11:49-07:00","id":855675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854920-how-does-umbra-combat-works?p=855576#post855576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It doesn't have an &quot;umbral form&quot;. It has a single form that has attributes in the umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is incorrect. They <u><b>must spend Essence</b></u> to use their other form in the umbra. As per &quot;<i>the spirit may take on a \u201cmore suitable\u201d combat form</i><i> <b><u>in the Umbra</u></b> <b>by spending</b> </i><i>Essence to build a body&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854920-how-does-umbra-combat-works?p=855576#post855576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is an immense boon for a spirit, as materialisation costs a stupid amount of essence, allowing these guys to have their whole essence pools</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">If they're dragged into the physical world this statement is true... but they have no way to get into the physical world by themselves. &quot;</span><i><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">They cannot Materialize, but if dragged into the physical world by other means, their forms are as physical as any mortal\u2019s.</span></i>&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Another question I just thought about<b></b>: If they use the physical form would they have 7 health levels or their full Essence pool?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:44:23-07:00","id":856247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>erSito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854920-how-does-umbra-combat-works?p=855675#post855675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is incorrect. They <u><b>must spend Essence</b></u> to use their other form in the umbra. As per &amp;quot;<i>the spirit may take on a \u201cmore suitable\u201d combat form</i><i> <b><u>in the Umbra</u></b> <b>by spending</b> </i><i>Essence to build a body&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">If they're dragged into the physical world this statement is true... but they have no way to get into the physical world by themselves. &amp;quot;</span><i><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">They cannot Materialize, but if dragged into the physical world by other means, their forms are as physical as any mortal\u2019s.</span></i>&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Another question I just thought about<b></b>: If they use the physical form would they have 7 health levels or their full Essence pool?<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What Asmodai is saying: the spirit does not need to use embody for the stat block. Embody is a charm to modify that body making it more combat effective.<br /> You are saying the spirit only gets the stat block after using embody. <br /> Given the &quot;weaker&quot; combat of the stat block as opposed to regular spirits I'm going to guess that Asmodai and the others have deciphered the intent of the author. If the spirit has a stat block body then armor would be active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T04:19:59-07:00","id":858876,"title":"","content":"W20 is a mess.<br /> This discussion is another example...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T12:19:55-07:00","id":862691,"title":"","content":"Oh curious in crossover, any ideas if I face a Vamp or psychic whos projecting? Defeating them sends a message, that their not welcome to spy on the garou, even if it doesnt kill them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T12:52:42-07:00","id":862710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/854920-how-does-umbra-combat-works?p=862691#post862691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh curious in crossover, any ideas if I face a Vamp or psychic whos projecting? Defeating them sends a message, that their not welcome to spy on the garou, even if it doesnt kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Projection sends you somewhere other than the Near Umbra, so it's a bit of a non-issue, usually. The rules came down on Garou and Fera visiting the High Umbra in W20, in addition to making it the High Umbra instead of a portion of the Deep Umbra..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}